</figure>
<div id="S4.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Unlike <em id="S4.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">m</em>AARS, we <em id="S4.SS2.p5.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">do not</em> take absolute values here. Because the metric captures the average year shift within the top-K segment, and our experimental design guarantees the segment has the lowest possible average year before date injection. Any values above zero indicates that the model favours newer passages, pulling fresher candidates into the top-K. Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.2. Average Year Shift in Top-K ‣ 4. Evaluation Metrics and Experiment Results ‣ Do Large Language Models Favor Recent Content? A Study on Recency Bias in LLM-Based Reranking" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> reports results for <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\!\in\!\{10,20,30,50\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\!\in\!\{10,20,30,50\}</annotation></semantics></math>, in which all values are statically significant at <math id="S4.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;0.05</annotation></semantics></math>, confirming our date-injection strategy consistently drives every LLM to promote passages with newer timestamps.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">GPT-4o and Qwen2.5-72B again prove most robust, while LLaMA3-8B is the most recency-sensitive, making the top-10 on average 4.780 years newer. All models show smaller shifts as <math id="S4.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> grows. For LLaMA3-8B, each of top-10 passages becomes 3.908 years fresher on DL21 and 4.780 years fresher on DL22. In comparison, the strongest models limit the shift to 0.819 years (Qwen2.5-72B on DL21) and 1.400 years (GPT-4o on DL22). When the cutoff widens to the top-50, the effect diminishes across the board, yet LLaMA3-8B still renders the list about a year newer (1.042 and 1.253 years). We attribute this attenuation at larger K to the dilution of extreme rank changes once the tail of the SERP is included.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3. </span>Average Year Shift by Groups</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To further analyse effect, we introduce another SERP-segment-level metric, <span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Average Year Shift by Groups</span> (<math id="S4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="YSG^{(g)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">YSG^{(g)}</annotation></semantics></math>), which quantifies temporal drift across different portions of the ranking. Each ranked list is divided into deciles (groups of ten). As with <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="YS^{(K)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">YS^{(K)}</annotation></semantics></math>, we <em id="S4.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">do not</em> take absolute values. In this setting, the average year for the middle segments, every decile except the first and last, can move in either direction. For the <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>-th (<math id="S4.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=0,\ldots,9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=0,\ldots,9</annotation></semantics></math>) group, covering positions <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[10g+1,10g+10]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[10g+1,10g+10]</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the average year shift as:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S4.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(8)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle YSG^{(g)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle YSG^{(g)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{|G_{g}|}\sum_{i\in G_{g}}\left(y_{i}^{\text{after}}-y_{i}^{\text{before}}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>after</mtext></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mtext>before</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{|G_{g}|}\sum_{i\in G_{g}}\left(y_{i}^{\text{after}}-y_{i}^{\text{before}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{g}=\{i\mid 10g+1\leq\text{rank}_{i}&lt;10g+11\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mtext>rank</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{g}=\{i\mid 10g+1\leq\text{rank}_{i}&lt;10g+11\}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the set of documents in group <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> based on their respective ranks. Grouping is applied independently before and after reranking.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Again, we report the mean value:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S4.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(9)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle mYSG^{(g)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle mYSG^{(g)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}YSG^{(g)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}YSG^{(g)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3. </span>Mean publication year shift by rank groups before and after date injection, on DL21 and DL22. Positive values are shown in bold. Entries marked with <sup id="S4.T3.4" class="ltx_sup">*</sup>are statistically significant at <math id="S4.T3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;0.05</annotation></semantics></math>. The <math id="S4.T3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-value is obtained from a <span id="S4.T3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">t-test</span>.</figcaption>
<div id="S4.T3.6" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:112.5pt;vertical-align:-54.8pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-129.3pt,42.2pt) scale(0.571521563627865,0.571521563627865) ;">
